# tools/agent_container/profiles/workstation.env -- the workstation's local-model server, reached over the LAN
# from homelab-server. UPDATED 2026-09-29: the serving bake-off (research/serving-bakeoff,
# tools/local_llm/results/summary.md) picked llama-server (74 tok/s, 3/3 tasks) over Ollama and Unsloth Studio,
# fronted by llama-swap for the "Serving simplification" pass (docs/plans/2026-09-29-local-model-transition-
# PLAN.md section 9) -- tools/local_llm/llama-swap.yaml now listens on 0.0.0.0 (LAN-reachable, not just
# 127.0.0.1 as the old direct llama-server launch did), which is what makes this profile reachable at all.
#
# BASE_URL/port: unchanged in form (llama-swap owns the same LLM_PORT, default 8080, tools/local_llm/llm.sh
# always used) -- only update the IP below if the workstation's LAN address changes.
# TOKEN_VAR left unset: llama-swap.yaml has no `apiKeys:` block (LAN is treated as trusted, same as the old
# unauthenticated llama-server) -- `llm` falls back to the same dummy "local" token tools/local_llm/llm.sh's own
# cmd_claude uses.
# MODEL=local: llama-swap.yaml's `profiles:` block pins this virtual id to whichever real profile.json entry
# `llm on <profile>` last selected on the workstation -- this container never needs to know the real name.
# CONTEXT=131072: tools/local_llm/default_profile's ctx (qwen38-27b-iq4nl-mtp-128k-q4, the bake-off winner).
# If the workstation's default profile ever changes, update this to match (`llm status` shows what is loaded).
BASE_URL=http://192.168.0.68:8080
TOKEN_VAR=
MODEL=local
CONTEXT=131072
KIND=local
